  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Algerian Delegation to the Netherlands for sustainable energy policy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In December 2023, the Netherlands hosted a distinguished Algerian delegation for a visit concerning renewable energy policy. This visit was part of an ongoing EU Twinning project jointly executed by the Netherlands and Germany, aimed at supporting renewable energy and energy efficiency in Algeria. It is co-facilitated by the CERF programme of the Netherlands Ministry of Foreign Affairs, implemented by RVO.The ten-member delegation comprised policymakers, technical experts, and representatives from various Algerian governmental institutions. Their objective was to understand Dutch efforts in sustainable energy policy, particularly on solar energy and green hydrogen. The Algerian delegation&apos;s visit, scheduled from December 3rd to 9th, included engagements with various Dutch institutions like RVO, PBL, TNO and ACM, focusing on climate policies, renewable energy, and regulatory aspects. The schedule also included visits to Delft and the Port of Amsterdam.</narrative>
  </description>
